#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1248
msgid "Bar Plots"
msgstr "Stapeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1252
msgid ""
"Bar plots present the numeric values of categorical data with the data "
"values of each series represented as a horizontal bar. Sequential data "
"values are considered to belong to different categories and are plotted "
"along the vertical axis at equally spaced intervals. The data values from "
"different series are assigned to these categories based on the position of "
"the value in the series, for example, the second data value taken from each "
"series all share one category. The data values are plotted along the "
"horizontal (X) axis as bars of different lengths and positions depending on "
"the numeric content of the data value and the particular sub-type chosen for"
" the bar plot."
msgstr ""
"Stapeldiagram visar numeriska värden för kategoridata som horisontella "
"staplar, en per värde i varje serie. Värden i följd hör till olika "
"kategorier och placeras med jämna mellanrum längs den vertikala axeln. "
"Värden från olika serier kopplas till kategorier utifrån sin position i "
"serien; det andra värdet i varje serie hör till exempel till samma kategori."
" Värdena visas som staplar längs den horisontella (X-)axeln. Staplarnas "
"längd och placering beror på värdet och den valda undertypen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1267
msgid ""
"Bar plot sub-types provide three options for relating the values from "
"different data series. The first sub-type plots each series independently in"
" adjacent bars, each of which is tied to the vertical axis and has its "
"length determined by the numeric content of the data value. The second sub-"
"type plots each series as a horizontally stacked set of bars with the "
"horizontal length of each element determined by the numeric content of the "
"data value and the position of the bar determined by the position of the "
"element in the data series. For example, if the first series starts with "
"values <literal>{3.9, 4.2, ...}</literal>, the second series with values "
"<literal>{1.2, 3.5, ...}</literal>, and the third series with values "
"<literal>{3.1, 1.9, ...}</literal>, then the third bar will be plotted "
"ranging from 7.7 to 9.6, since <literal>7.7=4.2+3.5</literal> and "
"<literal>9.6=4.2+3.5+1.9</literal>. The third sub-type plots each series as "
"a horizontally stacked set of bars scaled to the total all the numeric "
"values in that category. Using the example above, the three bars would range"
" from 0 to 0.4375, from 0.4375 to 0.8020, and from 0.8020 to 1 respectively "
"because the intervals are the proportional contribution of each data value "
"to the total, i.e. <literal>0.4375=4.2/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> for the "
"first, <literal>0.3645...=3.5/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> for the second, and "
"<literal>0.1979...=1.9/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> for the third. By default, "
"these numbers are presented as percentages on the horizontal (X) axis."
msgstr ""
"Undertyperna anger hur värden från olika dataserier förhåller sig till "
"varandra. Den första visar varje serie separat i staplar bredvid varandra. "
"Varje stapel utgår från den vertikala axeln och får sin längd av datavärdet."
" Den andra visar serierna som horisontellt staplade staplar. Varje dels "
"längd bestäms av datavärdet, och stapelns läge av dess position i serien. Om"
" den första serien till exempel börjar med värdena <literal>{3.9, 4.2, "
"...}</literal>, den andra med <literal>{1.2, 3.5, ...}</literal> och den "
"tredje med <literal>{3.1, 1.9, ...}</literal>, sträcker sig den tredje "
"stapeln från 7.7 till 9.6, eftersom <literal>7.7=4.2+3.5</literal> och "
"<literal>9.6=4.2+3.5+1.9</literal>. Den tredje undertypen visar serierna som"
" horisontellt staplade staplar, skalade efter summan av alla värden i "
"kategorin. Med exemplet ovan sträcker sig staplarna från 0 till 0.4375, från"
" 0.4375 till 0.8020 och från 0.8020 till 1. Intervallen motsvarar varje "
"datavärdes andel av summan: <literal>0.4375=4.2/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> för "
"den första, <literal>0.3645...=3.5/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> för den andra och"
" <literal>0.1979...=1.9/(4.2+3.5+1.9)</literal> för den tredje. Som standard"
" visas värdena som procentsatser på den horisontella (X-)axeln."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1301
msgid "Bar plots do not have any pre-defined styles."
msgstr "Stapeldiagram har inga fördefinierade stilar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1308
msgid "An example of bar plots"
msgstr "Exempel på stapeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1316
msgid ""
"A screenshot of a table of data and three bar plots made using those data."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbild av en datatabell och tre stapeldiagram som bygger på tabellens "
"värden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1322
msgid ""
"This screenshot shows a table of data and three bar plots. The data consist "
"of three series organized by row and starting with the words \"Widgets\", "
"\"Gadgets\", and \"Lumpets\". Each of these series has values in five "
"categories. The three graphs illustrate the three sub-types of bar plots, "
"with the series plotted independently in the left plot, stacked in the "
"middle plot, and proportionately stacked in the right plot."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar en datatabell och tre stapeldiagram. Data består av tre "
"radorienterade serier som börjar med etiketterna ”Widgets”, ”Gadgets” och "
"”Lumpets”. Varje serie innehåller värden för fem kategorier. Diagrammen "
"visar de tre undertyperna: serierna visas var för sig till vänster, staplade"
" i mitten och proportionellt staplade till höger."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1339
msgid ""
"Each series in bar plots can include three main elements and two error "
"elements, although only the value element is necessary. The series can have "
"a 'Name' element, which is a single text entry used to identify the series, "
"must have a 'Values' element, which is a sequence of numeric values, and may"
" have a 'Label' element, which is a sequence of text entries used to "
"identify the categories. All of these elements can be defined as references "
"to a region of the worksheet, as literally defined entries, or as formula "
"expressions which result in the correct type. The 'Label' element is shared "
"by all of the series. The legend added to a bar plot identifies the "
"different series, by default using the entries of the 'Name' element of each"
" series. The two error elements include a list for errors in the positive "
"direction and one for errors in the negative direction."
msgstr ""
"Varje dataserie i ett stapeldiagram kan innehålla tre huvudkomponenter och "
"två felkomponenter, men bara värdekomponenten är nödvändig. Serien kan ha "
"komponenten ”Namn”, ett textvärde som identifierar serien. Den måste ha "
"komponenten ”Värden”, en följd av numeriska värden, och kan även ha "
"komponenten ”Etikett”, en följd av textvärden som identifierar kategorierna."
" Komponenterna kan anges som referenser till ett område i kalkylbladet, som "
"fasta värden eller som formeluttryck som ger rätt datatyp. Alla serier delar"
" på komponenten ”Etikett”. Förklaringen till stapeldiagrammet identifierar "
"serierna och använder som standard värdena i respektive series komponent "
"”Namn”. De två felkomponenterna innehåller listor med positiva respektive "
"negativa felvärden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1357
msgid "The data in each bar plot series"
msgstr "Data i varje dataserie i ett stapeldiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1370
msgid ""
"A single textual element labeling the data series. These will be used in the"
" legend which may be displayed with the bar plot."
msgstr ""
"Ett textvärde som namnger dataserien. Det kan visas i stapeldiagrammets "
"förklaring."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1382
msgid ""
"A series of textual elements labeling each value. Generally, this series "
"will have as many entries as there were in the \"Value\" series. These "
"entries are shared by all the series in the bar plot."
msgstr ""
"En följd av textvärden som etiketterar varje värde. Följden innehåller "
"vanligen lika många poster som serien ”Värden”. Alla serier i "
"stapeldiagrammet delar på dessa etiketter."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:1408
msgid ""
"Bar plots provide three icons to choose one of the three bar plot sub-types."
msgstr "Tre ikoner motsvarar de tre undertyperna av stapeldiagram."

